<http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/Domain/CyberOntology> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "There are at least three unique senses of 'cyberspace': the interconnected physical devices that make up a telecommunication network; a space within those systems, presumably where electromagnetic energy flows; and the logical space of sequences and patterns of structured information carriers within that flow of energy. This last sense is analogous to the propagation of sound waves through the air or ripples in a pond and is closest to the view referred to within the defining elements of this ontology. However, all three may be applicable to articulate enties relevant to the cyber domain. Thus, we do not attempt to define 'cyberspace' formally and leave it as primitive. See Here: https://csrc.nist.gov/glossary/term/cyberspace."@en _:N88355ae2721847b3bb77370baee5ef13 .
