<http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/CybersecurityViolation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Cybersecurity Violations are differentiated from Cybersecurity Infractions because violations are specific to organizational policies. Not every act that violates a Cybersecurity Policy necessarily has a negative effect on the security of a Computer Network. Similarly, it is unlikely that any given Cybersecurity Policy is capable of documenting every possible action that would negatively affect a Computer Network. Hence, these classes are distinct despite having many instances in common."@en _:N88355ae2721847b3bb77370baee5ef13 .
